DG.put("ath-pakhyaan-charitr-likhyate/91",{"n":91,"title":null,"title_roman":null,"page":1347,"blocks":[{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":1347,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[1],"number_text":"੧।","page":1347,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਗਬਿੰਦ ਚੰਦ ਨਰੇਸ ਕੇ ਮਾਧਵਨਲ ਨਿਜੁ ਮੀਤ।","roman":"Gabind chand nares ke maadhavnal niju meet |","meaning_en":"King Gobind Chand had a close friend, Madhavanal,","page":1347,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਗੋਬਿੰਦ ਚੰਦ ਰਾਜੇ ਦਾ ਮਾਧਵਾਨਲ (ਨਾ ਦਾ ਇਕ) ਜਿਗਰੀ ਮਿੱਤਰ ਸੀ","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪੜੇ ਬ੍ਯਾਕਰਨ ਸ਼ਾਸਤ੍ਰ ਖਟ ਕੋਕ ਸਾਰ ਸੰਗੀਤ। ੧।","roman":"Pare byaakran shaasatr khat kok saar sangeet | 1 |","meaning_en":"who had studied grammar, the six shastras, the essence of the Kok (the art of love), and music.","page":1347,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕੋਕ: the Koka Shastra, a treatise on love.","meaning_pa":"ਜੋ ਵਿਆਕਰਣ ਖਟ-ਸ਼ਾਸਤ੍ਰ, ਕੋਕ ਸ਼ਾਸਤ੍ਰ ਅਤੇ ਸੰਗੀਤ ਪੜ੍ਰਹਦਾ ਸੀ ॥੧॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":1347,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੌਪਈ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[2],"number_text":"੨।","page":1347,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮਧੁਰ ਮਧੁਰ ਧੁਨਿ ਬੇਨੁ ਬਜਾਵੈ। ਜੋ ਕੋਊ ਤ੍ਰਿਯ ਸ੍ਰਵਨਨ ਸੁਨਿ ਪਾਵੈ।","roman":"Madhur madhur dhuni benu bajaavai | jo ko'oo triy sravnan suni paavai |","meaning_en":"He played the flute with a very sweet tune; any woman who heard it with her ears","page":1347,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਮਿਠੀ ਮਿਠੀ ਧੁਨ ਨਾਲ ਬੰਸਰੀ ਵਜਾਉਾਂਦਾ ਸੀ। (ਜਿਸ ਨੂੰ) ਜੇ ਕੋਈ ਇਸਤਰੀ ਕੰਨਾ ਨਾਲ ਸੁਣ ਲੈਂਦੀ","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚਿਤ ਮੈ ਅਧਿਕ ਮਤ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਝੂਲੈ। ਗ੍ਰਿਹ ਕੀ ਸਕਲ ਤਾਹਿ ਸੁਧਿ ਭੂਲੇ। ੨।","roman":"Chit mai adhik mat hvai jhoolai | grih kee sakal taahi sudhi bhoole | 2 |","meaning_en":"would sway at heart, greatly intoxicated, and forget all thought of her home.","page":1347,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤਾ ਚਿਤ ਵਿਚ ਅਧਿਕ ਮਸਤ ਹੋ ਕੇ ਝੂਮਦੀ। ਉਸ ਨੂੰ ਘਰ ਦੀ ਸਾਰੀ ਸੁੱਧ ਬੁੱਧ ਭੁਲ ਜਾਦੀ ॥੨॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[3],"number_text":"੩।","page":1347,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਪੁਰ ਬਾਸੀ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਪੈ ਚਲਿ ਆਏ। ਆਇ ਰਾਇ ਤਨ ਬਚਨ ਸੁਨਾਏ।","roman":"Pur baasee nrip pai chali aae | aai raai tan bachan sunaae |","meaning_en":"The townspeople came to the king, and, arriving, spoke these words to him:","page":1347,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸ਼ਹਿਰ ਦੇ ਨਿਵਾਸੀ ਰਾਜੇ ਕੋਲ ਚਲ ਕੇ ਆਏ ਅਤੇ ਆ ਕੇ ਰਾਜੇ ਪ੍ਰਤਿ ਬਚਨ ਕਹੇ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੈ ਮਾਧਵਨਲ ਕੌ ਅਬ ਮਰਿਯੈ। ਨਾ ਤੋ ਯਾ ਕਹ ਦੇਸ ਨਿਕਰਿਯੈ। ੩।","roman":"Kai maadhavnal kau ab mariyai | naa to yaa kah des nikriyai | 3 |","meaning_en":"\"Either have Madhavanal killed now, or else banish him from the country.","page":1347,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਾ ਤਾ ਮਾਧਵਾਨਲ ਨੂੰ ਹੁਣ ਮਾਰ ਦਿਓ, ਨਹੀਂ ਤਾ ਇਸ ਨੂੰ ਦੇਸ ਨਿਕਾਲਾ ਦੇ ਦਿਓ ॥੩॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":1349,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[4],"number_text":"੪।","page":1349,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਇਹ ਹਮਾਰੀ ਇਸਤ੍ਰੀਨ ਕੇ ਲੇਤ ਚਿਤ ਬਿਰਮਾਇ।","roman":"Ih hamaaree istreen ke let chit birmaai |","meaning_en":"He leads astray the hearts of our women;","page":1349,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਇਹ ਸਾਡੀਆਂ ਇਸਤਰੀਆਂ ਦੇ ਚਿਤ ਭਰਮਾ ਲੈਂਦਾ ਹੈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੌ ਹਮ ਸਭ ਕੌ ਕਾਢਿਯੈ ਤੌ ਇਹ ਰਖਿਯੈ ਰਾਹਿ। ੪।","roman":"Jau ham sabh kau kaadhiyai tau ih rakhiyai raahi | 4 |","meaning_en":"if you would drive all of us out, then keep him here.\"","page":1349,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਰਾਹਿ: read as 'here, in place'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਜਾ ਤਾ ਸਾਨੂੰ ਸਾਰਿਆਂ ਨੂੰ ਕਢ ਦਿਓ ਅਤੇ ਇਸ ਨੂੰ ਰਖ ਲਵੋ ॥੪॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":1349,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੌਪਈ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[5],"number_text":"੫।","page":1349,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤੋਰਿ ਰਾਵ ਤਬ ਜਲਜ ਮੰਗਾਏ। ਭਾਤਿ ਬਿਛੌਨਾ ਕੀ ਬਿਛਵਾਏ।","roman":"Tori raav tab jalaj mangaae | bhaati bichhaunaa kee bichhvaae |","meaning_en":"Then the king had lotuses plucked and brought, and had them spread out like a bedding.","page":1349,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤਦ ਰਾਜੇ ਨੇ ਕਮਲ ਫੁਲ ਤੁੜਵਾ ਕੇ ਮੰਗਵਾਏ ਅਤੇ ਵਿਛੌਣੇ ਵਾਗ ਵਿਛਵਾ ਦਿੱਤੇ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਕਲ ਸਖੀ ਤਿਹ ਪਰ ਬੈਠਾਈ। ਭਾਤਿ ਭਾਤਿ ਕੀ ਪ੍ਰਭਾ ਬਨਾਈ। ੫।","roman":"Sakal sakhee tih par baithaaee | bhaati bhaati kee prabhaa banaaee | 5 |","meaning_en":"He seated all the women on it and arranged a splendour of many kinds.","page":1349,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਖੀ: here 'women' generally.","meaning_pa":"ਉਸ ਉਤੇ ਸਾਰੀਆਂ ਸਖੀਆਂ ਬਿਠਾ ਦਿੱਤੀਆਂ ਤਰ੍ਰਹਾ ਤਰ੍ਰਹਾ ਦੇ ਸ਼ਿੰਗਾਰ ਕਰਵਾ ਕੇ ॥੫॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[6],"number_text":"੬।","page":1349,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮਾਧਵਨਲ ਕੌ ਬੋਲਿ ਪਠਾਇਸ। ਤਵਨ ਸਭਾ ਭੀਤਰ ਬੈਠਾਇਸ।","roman":"Maadhavnal kau boli pathaais | tavan sabhaa bheetar baithaais |","meaning_en":"He sent for Madhavanal and seated him within that assembly.","page":1349,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਤਾ ਉਸ ਨੇ) ਮਾਧਵਾਨਲ ਨੂੰ ਬੁਲਵਾ ਲਿਆ ਅਤੇ ਉਸ ਨੂੰ ਸਭਾ ਵਿਚ ਬਿਠਾਇਆ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰੀਝਿ ਬਿਪ੍ਰ ਤਬ ਬੇਨ ਬਜਾਈ। ਸਭ ਇਸਤ੍ਰਿਨ ਕੇ ਚਿਤ ਸੁ ਭਾਈ। ੬।","roman":"Reejhi bipr tab ben bajaaee | sabh istrin ke chit su bhaaee | 6 |","meaning_en":"Pleased, the brahmin then played the flute, and it delighted the hearts of all the women.","page":1349,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤਦ ਬ੍ਰਾਹਮਣ (ਮਾਧਵਾਨਲ) ਨੇ ਰੀਝ ਕੇ ਬੰਸਰੀ ਵਜਾਈ, ਜੋ ਸਾਰੀਆਂ ਇਸਤਰੀਆਂ ਦੇ ਮਨ ਨੂੰ ਚੰਗੀ ਲਗੀ ॥੬॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":1349,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[7],"number_text":"੭।","page":1349,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਭ ਅਬਲਾ ਮੋਹਿਤ ਭਈ ਨਾਦ ਸ੍ਰਵਨ ਸੁਨਿ ਪਾਇ।","roman":"Sabh ablaa mohit bhaee naad sravan suni paai |","meaning_en":"All the women were enchanted, hearing the sound with their ears;","page":1349,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕੰਨਾ ਨਾਲ ਉਸ ਧੁਨ ਨੂੰ ਸੁਣ ਕੇ ਸਾਰੀਆਂ ਇਸਤਰੀਆ ਮੋਹਿਤ ਹੋ ਗਈਆਂ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਭਹਿਨ ਕੇ ਤਨ ਸੌ ਗਏ ਕਮਲ ਪਤ੍ਰ ਲਪਟਾਇ। ੭।","roman":"Sabhhin ke tan sau gae kamal patr laptaai | 7 |","meaning_en":"the lotus leaves clung to the bodies of every one of them.","page":1349,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸਾਰੀਆਂ ਦੇ ਸ਼ਰੀਰ ਨਾਲ ਕਮਲ ਦੇ ਪੱਤੇ ਚਿਪਕ ਗਏ ॥੭॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":1349,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੌਪਈ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[8],"number_text":"੮।","page":1349,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮਾਧਵਨਲ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਤੁਰਤੁ ਨਿਕਾਰਿਯੋ। ਬਿਪ੍ਰ ਜਾਨਿ ਜਿਯ ਤੇ ਨਹੀ ਮਾਰਿਯੋ।","roman":"Maadhavnal nrip turtu nikaariyo | bipr jaani jiy te nahee maariyo |","meaning_en":"The king at once banished Madhavanal; knowing him to be a brahmin, he did not kill him.","page":1349,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਮਾਧਵਾਨਲ ਨੂੰ ਰਾਜੇ ਨੇ ਤੁਰਤ ਕੱਢ ਦਿੱਤਾ, ਪਰ ਬ੍ਰਾਹਮਣ ਜਾਣ ਕੇ ਜਾਨੋ ਨਹੀਂ ਮਾਰਿਆ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਮਾਵਤੀ ਨਗਰ ਚਲਿ ਆਯੋ। ਕਾਮਕੰਦਲਾ ਸੌ ਹਿਤ ਭਾਯੋ। ੮।","roman":"Kaamaavtee nagar chali aayo | kaamkandlaa sau hit bhaayo | 8 |","meaning_en":"He came to the city of Kamavati, and came to love Kamakandla.","page":1349,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਉਹ ਉਥੋਂ) ਚਲ ਕੇ ਕਾਮਾਵਤੀ ਨਗਰੀ ਵਿਚ ਆ ਗਿਆ। (ਉਥੇ ਆ ਕੇ ਉਸ ਦਾ) ਕਾਮਕੰਦਲਾ ਨਾਲ ਹਿਤ ਹੋ ਗਿਆ ॥੮॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":1349,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[9],"number_text":"੯।","page":1349,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਮ ਸੈਨ ਰਾਜਾ ਜਹਾ ਤਹ ਦਿਜ ਪਹੂੰਚ੍ਯੋ ਜਾਇ।","roman":"Kaam sain raajaa jahaa tah dij pahoonchyo jaai |","meaning_en":"The brahmin arrived where King Kam Sen was,","page":1349,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਿਥੇ ਕਾਮ ਸੈਨ ਨਾ ਦਾ ਰਾਜਾ ਸੀ, ਬ੍ਰਾਹਮਣ (ਮਾਧਵਾਨਲ) ਉਥੇ ਜਾ ਪਹੁੰਚਿਆ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪ੍ਰਗਟ ਤੀਨਿ ਸੈ ਸਾਠਿ ਤ੍ਰਿਯ ਨਾਚਤ ਜਹਾ ਬਨਾਇ। ੯।","roman":"Pragat teeni sai saathi triy naachat jahaa banaai | 9 |","meaning_en":"where three hundred and sixty women danced openly, finely adorned.","page":1349,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਥੇ (ਰਾਜੇ ਦੇ) ਸਾਹਮਣੇ ੩੬੦ ਇਸਤਰੀਆਂ ਨਾਚ ਕਰਦੀਆਂ ਹੁੰਦੀਆਂ ਸਨ ॥੯॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":1349,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੌਪਈ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[10],"number_text":"੧੦।","page":1349,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮਾਧਵ ਤੌਨ ਸਭਾ ਮਹਿ ਆਯੋ। ਆਨਿ ਰਾਵ ਕੌ ਸੀਸ ਝੁਕਾਯੋ।","roman":"Maadhav taun sabhaa mahi aayo | aani raav kau sees jhukaayo |","meaning_en":"Madhav came into that court and bowed his head to the king.","page":1349,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਮਾਧਵਾਨਲ ਉਸ ਦੀ ਸਭਾ ਵਿਚ ਆਇਆ ਅਤੇ ਆ ਕੇ ਰਾਜੇ ਨੂੰ ਸੀਸ ਝੁਕਾਇਆ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੂਰਬੀਰ ਬੈਠੇ ਬਹੁ ਜਹਾ। ਨਾਚਤ ਕਾਮਕੰਦਲਾ ਤਹਾ। ੧੦।","roman":"Soorbeer baithe bahu jahaa | naachat kaamkandlaa tahaa | 10 |","meaning_en":"Where many brave warriors sat, there Kamakandla was dancing.","page":1349,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਿਥੇ ਬਹੁਤ ਸੂਰਬੀਰ ਬੈਠੇ ਹੋਏ ਸਨ, ਉਥੇ ਕਾਮਕੰਦਲਾ ਨਚ ਰਹੀ ਸੀ ॥੧੦॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":1349,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[11],"number_text":"੧੧।","page":1349,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਚੰਦਨ ਕੀ ਤਨ ਕੰਚੁਕੀ ਕਾਮਾ ਕਸੀ ਬਨਾਇ।","roman":"Chandan kee tan kanchukee kaamaa kasee banaai |","meaning_en":"Kama had made a bodice of sandal paste upon her body and fastened it on;","page":1349,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਾਮਾ: short for Kamakandla.","meaning_pa":"ਕਾਮਕੰਦਲਾ ('ਕਾਮਾ') ਨੇ ਚੰਦਨ ਦੀ ਅੰਗੀ ('ਕੰਚੁਕੀ') ਚੰਗੀ ਤਰ੍ਰਹਾ ਕਸੀ ਹੋਈ ਸੀ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅੰਗਿਯਾ ਹੀ ਸਭ ਕੋ ਲਖੈ ਚੰਦਨ ਲਖ੍ਯੋ ਨ ਜਾਇ। ੧੧।","roman":"Angiyaa hee sabh ko lakhai chandan lakhyo na jaai | 11 |","meaning_en":"everyone saw it only as a bodice; that it was sandal could not be seen.","page":1349,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸਭ ਨੂੰ ਅੰਗੀ ਹੀ ਨਜ਼ਰ ਆਉਾਂਦੀ ਸੀ, ਚੰਦਨ ਨਹੀਂ ਦਿਖਦਾ ਸੀ ॥੧੧॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[12],"number_text":"੧੨।","page":1349,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਚੰਦਨ ਕੀ ਲੈ ਬਾਸਨਾ ਭਵਰ ਬਹਿਠ੍ਯੋ ਆਇ।","roman":"Chandan kee lai baasnaa bhavar bahithyo aai |","meaning_en":"Drawn by the scent of the sandal, a bee came and settled on it;","page":1349,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੰਦਨ ਦੀ ਵਾਸਨਾ ਲੈ ਕੇ ਭੌਰਾ (ਉਥੇ) ਆ ਬੈਠਿਆ","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੋ ਤਿਨ ਕੁਚ ਕੀ ਬਾਯੁ ਤੇ ਦੀਨੌ ਤਾਹਿ ਉਠਾਇ। ੧੨।","roman":"So tin kuch kee baayu te deenau taahi uthaai | 12 |","meaning_en":"she drove it off with the breath of her breasts.","page":1349,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕੁਚ ਕੀ ਬਾਯੁ: literally 'the air of the breasts', i.e. by a movement of the breast; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਜਿਸ ਨੂੰ ਉਸ ਨੇ ਛਾਤੀਆਂ (ਦੇ ਝਟਕੇ ਤੋ ਪੈਦਾ ਕੀਤੀ) ਹਵਾ ਨਾਲ ਉਡਾ ਦਿੱਤਾ ॥੧੨॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":1349,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੌਪਈ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[13],"number_text":"੧੩।","page":1349,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਇਹ ਸੁ ਭੇਦ ਬਿਪ ਨੈ ਲਹਿ ਲਯੋ। ਰੀਝਤ ਅਧਿਕ ਚਿਤ ਮਹਿ ਭਯੋ।","roman":"Ih su bhed bip nai lahi layo | reejhat adhik chit mahi bhayo |","meaning_en":"The brahmin perceived this secret, and was greatly delighted at heart.","page":1349,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਇਹ ਸਾਰਾ ਭੇਦ ਬ੍ਰਾਹਮਣ ਨੇ ਸਮਝ ਲਿਆ। (ਉਹ) ਮਨ ਵਿਚ ਬਹੁਤ ਪ੍ਰਸੰਨ ਹੋਇਆ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਮਿਤ ਦਰਬੁ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਤੇ ਜੋ ਲੀਨੋ। ਸੋ ਲੈ ਕਾਮਕੰਦਲਹਿ ਦੀਨੋ। ੧੩।","roman":"Amit darbu nrip te jo leeno | so lai kaamkandalhi deeno | 13 |","meaning_en":"The boundless wealth he had received from the king, he took and gave to Kamakandla.","page":1349,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਉਸ ਨੇ) ਜੋ ਬਹੁਤ ਸਾਰਾ ਧਨ ਰਾਜੇ ਤੋਂ ਲਿਆ ਸੀ, ਉਹ (ਉਸ ਨੇ) ਲੈ ਕੇ ਕਾਮਕੰਦਲਾ ਨੂੰ ਦੇ ਦਿੱਤਾ ॥੧੩॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":1351,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[14],"number_text":"੧੪।","page":1351,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਮਿਤ ਦਰਬੁ ਹਮ ਜੋ ਦਯੋ ਸੋ ਇਹ ਦਯੋ ਲੁਟਾਇ।","roman":"Amit darbu ham jo dayo so ih dayo lutaai |","meaning_en":"\"The boundless wealth I gave, he has squandered;","page":1351,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"The king is speaking.","meaning_pa":"(ਰਾਜੇ ਸੋਚਿਆ) ਅਸੀਂ ਇਸ ਨੂੰ ਜੋ ਬੇਹਿਸਾਬਾ ਧਨ ਦਿੱਤਾ ਸੀ, ਉਹ (ਇਸ ਨੇ) ਲੁਟਾ ਦਿੱਤਾ ਹੈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਐਸੇ ਬਿਪ੍ਰ ਫਜੂਲ ਕੋ ਮੋਹਿ ਨ ਰਾਖ੍ਯੋ ਜਾਇ। ੧੪।","roman":"Aise bipr phajool ko mohi na raakhyo jaai | 14 |","meaning_en":"such a wasteful brahmin I cannot keep.","page":1351,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਫਜੂਲ: Persian/Arabic fuzul, 'wasteful, extravagant'.","meaning_pa":"ਅਜਿਹੇ ਫ਼ਜ਼ੂਲ ਖ਼ਰਚ ਬ੍ਰਾਹਮਣ ਨੂੰ ਮੇਰੇ ਕੋਲੋਂ ਨਹੀਂ ਰਖਿਆ ਜਾਦਾ ॥੧੪॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":1351,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੌਪਈ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[15],"number_text":"੧੫।","page":1351,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਿਪ੍ਰ ਜਾਨਿ ਜਿਯ ਤੇ ਨਹਿ ਮਰਿਯੈ। ਇਹ ਪੁਰ ਤੇ ਇਹ ਤੁਰਤੁ ਨਿਕਰਿਯੈ।","roman":"Bipr jaani jiy te nahi mariyai | ih pur te ih turtu nikriyai |","meaning_en":"Knowing him a brahmin, he is not to be killed; drive him out of this city at once.","page":1351,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਬ੍ਰਾਹਮਣ ਜਾਣ ਕੇ (ਇਸ ਨੂੰ) ਜਾਨ ਤੋਂ ਨਹੀਂ ਮਾਰਨਾ ਚਾਹੀਦਾ, ਪਰ ਇਸ ਨੂੰ ਇਸ ਨਗਰ ਤੋਂ ਤੁਰਤ ਕਢ ਦੇਣਾ ਚਾਹੀਦਾ ਹੈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਾ ਕੇ ਦੁਰਿਯੋ ਧਾਮ ਲਹਿ ਲੀਜੈ। ਟੂਕ ਅਨੇਕ ਤਵਨ ਕੋ ਕੀਜੈ। ੧੫।","roman":"Jaa ke duriyo dhaam lahi leejai | took anek tavan ko keejai | 15 |","meaning_en":"Whoever's house he is found hiding in, cut that person into many pieces.\"","page":1351,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਇਹ ਵੀ ਕਹਿ ਦਿੱਤਾ ਕਿ) ਜਿਸ ਦੇ ਘਰ ਵਿਚ ਇਹ ਲੁਕਿਆ ਹੋਇਆ ਮਿਲਿਆ, ਉਸ ਦੇ ਅਨੇਕ ਟੋਟੇ ਕਰ ਦਿੱਤੇ ਜਾਣ ॥੧੫॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[16],"number_text":"੧੬।","page":1351,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਯਹ ਸਭ ਭੇਦ ਬਿਪ੍ਰ ਸੁਨਿ ਪਾਯੋ। ਚਲਿਯੋ ਚਲਿਯੋ ਕਾਮਾ ਗ੍ਰਿਹ ਆਯੋ।","roman":"Yah sabh bhed bipr suni paayo | chaliyo chaliyo kaamaa grih aayo |","meaning_en":"The brahmin heard all this; going on and on, he came to Kama's house:","page":1351,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਇਹ ਸਾਰੀ ਗੱਲ ਬ੍ਰਾਹਮਣ ਨੇ ਸੁਣ ਲਈ। ਉਹ ਚਲਦਾ ਚਲਦਾ ਕਾਮਕੰਦਲਾ ਦੇ ਘਰ ਆਇਆ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮੋ ਪਰ ਕੋਪ ਅਧਿਕ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਕੀਨੋ। ਤਿਹ ਹਿਤ ਧਾਮ ਤਿਹਾਰੋ ਚੀਨੋ। ੧੬।","roman":"Mo par kop adhik nrip keeno | tih hit dhaam tihaaro cheeno | 16 |","meaning_en":"\"The king has become very angry with me; that is why I have sought out your house.\"","page":1351,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਕਹਿਣ ਲਗਿਆ ਕਿ) ਮੇਰੇ ਉਤੇ ਰਾਜੇ ਨੇ ਬਹੁਤ ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਕੀਤਾ ਹੈ। ਇਸ ਲਈ ਤੇਰਾ ਘਰ ਲਭਿਆ ਹੈ ॥੧੬॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":1351,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[17],"number_text":"੧੭।","page":1351,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਨਤ ਬਚਨ ਕਾਮਾ ਤੁਰਤ ਦਿਜ ਗ੍ਰਿਹ ਲਯੋ ਦੁਰਾਇ।","roman":"Sunat bachan kaamaa turat dij grih layo duraai |","meaning_en":"Hearing these words, Kama at once hid the brahmin in her house;","page":1351,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਾਮਕੰਦਲਾ ਨੇ ਬਚਨ ਸੁਣ ਕੇ ਤੁਰਤ ਬ੍ਰਾਹਮਣ ਨੂੰ ਘਰ ਵਿਚ ਲੁਕਾ ਲਿਆ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰਾਜਾ ਕੀ ਨਿੰਦ੍ਯਾ ਕਰੀ ਤਾਹਿ ਗਰੇ ਸੋ ਲਾਇ। ੧੭।","roman":"Raajaa kee nindyaa karee taahi gare so laai | 17 |","meaning_en":"she reviled the king and held him to her bosom.","page":1351,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਸ ਨੂੰ ਗਲੇ ਨਾਲ ਲਾ ਕੇ ਰਾਜੇ ਦੀ ਨਿੰਦਿਆ ਕੀਤੀ ॥੧੭॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਕਾਮਾ ਬਾਚ","gurmukhi":"ਕਾਮਾ ਬਾਚ","roman":"Kaamaa baach","meaning_en":"Kama said:","page":1351,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਾਮਕੰਦਲਾ ਨੇ ਕਿਹਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":1351,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੌਪਈ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[18],"number_text":"੧੮।","page":1351,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਧ੍ਰਿਗ ਇਹ ਰਾਇ ਭੇਦ ਨਹਿ ਜਾਨਤ। ਤੁਮ ਸੇ ਚਤੁਰਨ ਸੌ ਰਿਸਿ ਠਾਨਤ।","roman":"Dhrig ih raai bhed nahi jaanat | tum se chaturan sau risi thaanat |","meaning_en":"\"Shame on this king, who does not understand the secret, and is angry with clever men like you.","page":1351,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਇਸ ਰਾਜੇ ਨੂੰ ਧਿੱਕਾਰ ਹੈ ਜੋ ਭੇਦ ਨੂੰ ਨਹੀਂ ਜਾਣਦਾ। ਤੁਹਾਡੇ ਵਰਗੇ ਸੂਝਵਾਨ ਉਤੇ ਨਾਰਾਜ਼ ਹੁੰਦਾ ਹੈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਹਾ ਮੂੜ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਕੋ ਕਾ ਕਹਿਯੈ। ਯਾ ਪਾਪੀ ਕੇ ਦੇਸ ਨ ਰਹਿਯੈ। ੧੮।","roman":"Mahaa moor nrip ko kaa kahiyai | yaa paapee ke des na rahiyai | 18 |","meaning_en":"What can be said of such a great fool of a king? One should not stay in this sinner's country.","page":1351,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅਜਿਹੇ ਮਹਾ ਮੂਰਖ ਰਾਜੇ ਨੂੰ ਕੀ ਕਹੀਏ। ਇਸ ਪਾਪੀ ਦੇ ਦੇਸ ਨਹੀਂ ਰਹਿਣਾ ਚਾਹੀਦਾ ॥੧੮॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":1351,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[19],"number_text":"੧੯।","page":1351,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਚਲੌ ਤ ਏਕੈ ਮਗੁ ਚਲੌ ਰਹੇ ਰਹੌ ਤਿਹ ਗਾਉ।","roman":"Chalau ta ekai magu chalau rahe rahau tih gaau |","meaning_en":"If you go, I go by the same road; if you stay, I stay in that village;","page":1351,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜੇ ਚਲੋਗੇ ਤਾ (ਤੁਹਾਡੇ ਨਾਲ) ਇਕੋ ਮਾਰਗ ਉਤੇ ਚਲਾਗੀ, (ਜਿਥੇ) ਰਹੋਗੇ, ਉਸ ਪਿੰਡ ਵਿਚ ਰਹਾਗੀ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਿਸੁ ਦਿਨ ਰਟੌ ਬਿਹੰਗ ਜ੍ਯੋ ਮੀਤ ਤਿਹਾਰੋ ਨਾਉ। ੧੯।","roman":"Nisu din ratau bihang jyo meet tihaaro naau | 19 |","meaning_en":"night and day, like a bird, I will repeat your name, my friend.","page":1351,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਰਾਤ ਦਿਨ ਪੰਛੀ (ਪਪੀਹੇ) ਵਾਗ ਹੇ ਮਿੱਤਰ! ਤੇਰਾ ਨਾਮ ਜਪਾਗੀ ॥੧੯॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[20],"number_text":"੨੦।","page":1351,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਿਰਹ ਬਾਨ ਮੋ ਤਨ ਗਡੇ ਕਾ ਸੋ ਕਰੋ ਪੁਕਾਰ।","roman":"Birah baan mo tan gade kaa so karo pukaar |","meaning_en":"The arrows of separation are lodged in my body; to whom shall I cry out?","page":1351,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਵਿਯੋਗ ਦਾ ਬਾਣ ਮੇਰੇ ਸ਼ਰੀਰ ਵਿਚ ਲਗਾ ਹੈ, ਕਿਸ ਅਗੇ ਪੁਕਾਰ ਕਰਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਨਕ ਅਗਨਿ ਕੋ ਸਿਵ ਭਏ ਜਰੌ ਸੰਭਾਰਿ ਸੰਭਾਰਿ। ੨੦।","roman":"Tanak agni ko siv bhae jarau sanbhaari sanbhaari | 20 |","meaning_en":"even Shiva was undone by a little fire; I burn, remembering again and again.","page":1351,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Obscure line. ਤਨਕ ਅਗਨਿ ਕੋ ਸਿਵ ਭਏ: possibly an allusion to Shiva and the fire (of Kam); reading uncertain. ਸੰਭਾਰਿ ਸੰਭਾਰਿ: 'recalling again and again' or 'bearing it carefully'.","meaning_pa":"ਥੋੜੀ ਜਿਹੀ ਅਗਨੀ ਦਾ ਸਿਵਾ ਬਣ ਗਿਆ ਹੈ, ਹੌਲੀ ਹੌਲੀ ਸੜ ਰਹੀ ਹਾ ॥੨੦॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[21],"number_text":"੨੧।","page":1351,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਆਜੁ ਸਖੀ ਮੈ ਯੌ ਸੁਨ੍ਯੋ ਪਹੁ ਫਾਟਤ ਪਿਯ ਗੌਨ।","roman":"Aaju sakhee mai yau sunyo pahu phaatat piy gaun |","meaning_en":"Today, friend, I have heard that at break of dawn my beloved departs;","page":1351,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਆਪਣੇ ਆਪ ਨਾਲ ਗੱਲ ਕਰਦੀ ਹੋਈ ਕਹਿੰਦੀ ਹੈ) ਹੇ ਸਖੀ! ਅਜ ਮੈਂ ਇਹ ਸੁਣਿਆ ਹੈ ਕਿ ਪਹੁ ਫੁਟਾਲੇ ਨਾਲ ਪ੍ਰੀਤਮ ਚਲੇ ਜਾਣਗੇ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਹੁ ਹਿਯਰੇ ਝਗਰਾ ਪਰਿਯੋ ਪਹਿਲੇ ਫਟਿ ਹੈ ਕੌਨ। ੨੧।","roman":"Pahu hiyre jhagraa pariyo pahile phati hai kaun | 21 |","meaning_en":"a quarrel has arisen between the dawn and my heart, which will break first.","page":1351,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Wordplay on ਫਾਟਤ/ਫਟਿ: the dawn 'breaks' and the heart 'breaks'.","meaning_pa":"(ਮੇਰੇ) ਹਿਰਦੇ ਵਿਚ ਝਗੜਾ ਚਲ ਰਿਹਾ ਹੈ ਕਿ ਪਹਿਲਾ ਕੋਣ ਫਟੇਗਾ? (ਪਹੁ ਫੁਟਾਲਾ ਹੋਵੇਗਾ ਜਾ ਮੇਰਾ ਹਿਰਦਾ ਫਟੇਗਾ) ॥੨੧॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਮਾਧਵ ਬਾਚ","gurmukhi":"ਮਾਧਵ ਬਾਚ","roman":"Maadhav baach","meaning_en":"Madhav said:","page":1351,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਮਾਧਵਾਨਲ ਨੇ ਕਿਹਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":1351,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੌਪਈ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[22],"number_text":"੨੨।","page":1351,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤੁਮ ਸੁਖ ਸੋ ਸੁੰਦਰਿ ਹ੍ਯਾ ਰਹੋ। ਹਮ ਕੋ ਬੇਗਿ ਬਿਦਾ ਮੁਖ ਕਹੋ।","roman":"Tum sukh so sundri hyaa raho | ham ko begi bidaa mukh kaho |","meaning_en":"\"Fair one, stay here in comfort; quickly bid me farewell with your own mouth.","page":1351,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹੇ ਸੁੰਦਰੀ! ਤੁਸੀਂ ਸੁਖ ਨਾਲ ਇਥੇ ਰਹੋ ਅਤੇ ਸਾਨੂੰ ਜਲਦੀ ਨਾਲ ਮੁਖ ਤੋਂ ਵਿਦਾ ਕਹੋ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹਮਰੋ ਕਛੂ ਤਾਪ ਨਹ ਕਰਿਯਹੁ। ਨਿਤ ਰਾਮ ਕੋ ਨਾਮ ਸੰਭਰਿਯਹੁ। ੨੨।","roman":"Hamro kachhoo taap nah kariyhu | nit raam ko naam sanbhriyhu | 22 |","meaning_en":"Do not grieve for me at all; always remember the Name of Ram.\"","page":1351,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸਾਡੇ (ਜਾਣ ਦਾ) ਕੋਈ ਦੁਖ ਨਹੀਂ ਮੰਨਣਾ ਅਤੇ ਨਿੱਤ ਰਾਮ ਦੇ ਨਾਮ ਦੀ ਅਰਾਧਨਾ ਕਰਨਾ ॥੨੨॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":1351,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[23],"number_text":"੨੩।","page":1351,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਨਤ ਬਚਨ ਕਾਮਾ ਤਬੈ ਭੂਮਿ ਪਰੀ ਮੁਰਛਾਇ।","roman":"Sunat bachan kaamaa tabai bhoomi paree murchhaai |","meaning_en":"Hearing these words, Kama then fell fainting to the ground,","page":1351,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਾਮਕੰਦਲਾ (ਮਾਧਵਾਨਲ ਦੇ) ਬਚਨ ਸੁਣ ਕੇ ਬੇਹੋਸ਼ ਹੋ ਕੇ ਧਰਤੀ ਉਤੇ ਡਿਗ ਪਈ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਨੁ ਘਾਯਲ ਘਾਇਨ ਲਗੇ ਗਿਰੈ ਉਠੈ ਬਰਰਾਇ। ੨੩।","roman":"Janu ghaayal ghaain lage girai uthai barraai | 23 |","meaning_en":"like a wounded warrior struck by blows, who falls, rises, and raves.","page":1351,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਮਾਨੋ ਘਾਇਲ ਘਾਉ ਲਗਣ ਤੇ ਡਿਗਦਾ, ਉਠਦਾ ਅਤੇ ਬਰੜਾਉਾਂਦਾ ਹੋਵੇ ॥੨੩॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸੋਰਠਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸੋਰਠਾ","roman":"Sorthaa","meaning_en":"Sortha.","page":1353,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸੋਰਠਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[24],"number_text":"੨੪।","page":1353,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਧਿਕ ਬਿਰਹ ਕੇ ਸੰਗ ਪੀਤ ਬਰਨ ਕਾਮਾ ਭਈ।","roman":"Adhik birah ke sang peet baran kaamaa bhaee |","meaning_en":"With great pangs of separation Kama turned pale yellow;","page":1353,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅਧਿਕ ਵਿਯੋਗ ਕਾਰਨ ਕਾਮਕੰਦਲਾ ਦਾ ਰੰਗ ਪੀਲਾ ਪੈ ਗਿਆ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰਕਤ ਨ ਰਹਿਯੋ ਅੰਗ ਚਲਿਯੋ ਮੀਤ ਚੁਰਾਇ ਚਿਤ। ੨੪।","roman":"Rakat na rahiyo ang chaliyo meet churaai chit | 24 |","meaning_en":"no blood remained in her limbs; her friend went away, stealing her heart.","page":1353,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਉਸ ਦੇ) ਸ਼ਰੀਰ ਵਿਚ ਲਹੂ ਨਹੀਂ ਰਿਹਾ (ਕਿਉਾਂਕਿ ਉਸ ਦਾ) ਮਿੱਤਰ ਦਿਲ ਚੁਰਾ ਕੇ ਚਲਾ ਗਿਆ ਹੈ ॥੨੪॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":1353,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[25],"number_text":"੨੫।","page":1353,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਟਾਂਕ ਤੋਲ ਤਨ ਨ ਰਹਿਯੋ ਮਾਸਾ ਰਹਿਯੋ ਨ ਮਾਸ।","roman":"Taank tol tan na rahiyo maasaa rahiyo na maas |","meaning_en":"Not a tank's weight remained in her body, not a masha of flesh;","page":1353,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਟਾਂਕ, ਮਾਸਾ: small units of weight; wordplay on ਮਾਸਾ (a weight) and ਮਾਸ (flesh)."},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਿਰਹਿਨ ਕੌ ਤੀਨੋ ਭਲੇ ਹਾਡ ਚਾਮ ਅਰੁ ਸ੍ਵਾਸ। ੨੫।","roman":"Birhin kau teeno bhale haad chaam aru svaas | 25 |","meaning_en":"for a woman in separation three things are left: bone, skin and breath.","page":1353,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਭਲੇ: literally 'good'; here taken as 'are what remain'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਚਾਰ ਮਾਸੇ ਸ਼ਰੀਰ ਨਹੀਂ ਰਿਹਾ ਅਤੇ ਮਾਸਾ ਜਿੰਨਾ ਵੀ ਮਾਸ ਨਹੀਂ ਰਿਹਾ। ਵਿਯੋਗਣਾ ਲਈ ਹਡ, ਚੰਮ ਅਤੇ ਸੁਆਸ ਤਿੰਨੇ (ਰੋਗ) ਚੰਗੇ ਹਨ ॥੨੫॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB","note_pa":"ਇਹ ਅਰਥ ਇਸ ਪੰਕਤੀ ਸਮੇਤ ਉੱਪਰਲੀਆਂ 2 ਪੰਕਤੀਆਂ ਦਾ ਇਕੱਠਾ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[26],"number_text":"੨੬।","page":1353,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਤਿ ਕਾਮਾ ਲੋਟਤ ਧਰਨਿ ਮਾਧਵਨਲ ਕੇ ਹੇਤ।","roman":"Ati kaamaa lotat dharni maadhavnal ke het |","meaning_en":"Kama rolled on the ground in great distress for Madhavanal,","page":1353,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਮਾਧਵਾਨਲ ਦੇ ਹਿਤ ਲਈ ਕਾਮਕੰਦਲਾ ਧਰਤੀ ਉਤੇ ਲੋਟ ਪੋਟ ਹੋ ਰਹੀ ਹੈ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਟੂਟੋ ਅਮਲ ਅਫੀਮਿਯਹਿ ਜਨੁ ਪਸਵਾਰੇ ਲੇਤ। ੨੬।","roman":"Tooto amal apheemiyhi janu pasvaare let | 26 |","meaning_en":"as an opium-eater whose habit is broken tosses from side to side.","page":1353,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਟੂਟੋ ਅਮਲ: the craving when the dose is missed. ਪਸਵਾਰੇ ਲੇਤ: 'turns from side to side'.","meaning_pa":"ਮਾਨੋ ਅਮਲ ਤੋਂ ਟੁਟਿਆ ਅਫ਼ੀਮਚੀ ਪਲਸੇਟੇ ਮਾਰ ਰਿਹਾ ਹੋਵੇ ॥੨੬॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[27],"number_text":"੨੭।","page":1353,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮਿਲਤ ਨੈਨ ਨਹਿ ਰਹਿ ਸਕਤ ਜਾਨਤ ਪ੍ਰੀਤਿ ਪਤੰਗ।","roman":"Milat nain nahi rahi sakat jaanat preeti patang |","meaning_en":"When eyes meet they cannot hold back; the moth knows what love is:","page":1353,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਪਤੰਗ (ਦੀਪਕ ਨਾਲ ਪਾਈ) ਪ੍ਰੀਤ ਤੋਂ ਜਾਣ ਸਕਦਾ ਹੈ ਕਿ ਨੈਣ ਮਿਲਾਏ ਬਿਨਾ ਰਿਹਾ ਨਹੀਂ ਜਾ ਸਕਦਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਛੂਟਤ ਬਿਰਹ ਬਿਯੋਗ ਤੇ ਹੋਮਤ ਅਪਨੋ ਅੰਗ। ੨੭।","roman":"Chhootat birah biyog te homat apno ang | 27 |","meaning_en":"to be freed from the pain of separation, it offers its own body into the fire.","page":1353,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਹੋਮਤ: offers as an oblation.","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਵਿਰਹ ਵਿਯੋਗ ਕਾਰਨ (ਦੀਪਕ ਨੂੰ) ਛੋਹ ਕੇ ਆਪਣੇ ਅੰਗ ਸਾੜ (ਹੋਮ ਕਰ) ਦਿੰਦਾ ਹੈ ॥੨੭॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਕਾਮਾ ਬਾਚ","gurmukhi":"ਕਾਮਾ ਬਾਚ","roman":"Kaamaa baach","meaning_en":"Kama said:","page":1353,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਾਮਕੰਦਲਾ ਨੇ ਕਿਹਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":1353,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੌਪਈ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[28],"number_text":"੨੮।","page":1353,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਖੰਡ ਖੰਡ ਕੈ ਤੀਰਥ ਕਰਿਹੌ। ਬਾਰਿ ਅਨੇਕ ਆਗਿ ਮੈ ਬਰਿਹੌ।","roman":"Khand khand kai teerath karihau | baari anek aagi mai barihau |","meaning_en":"\"I will go on pilgrimage in every region; many times I will burn myself in fire;","page":1353,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਮੈਂ) ਸਾਰਿਆਂ ਖੰਡਾ ਦੇ ਤੀਰਥਾ ਤੇ ਜਾਵਾਗੀ। ਅਨੇਕ ਵਾਰ ਅਗਨੀ ਵਿਚ ਸੜਾਗੀ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਸੀ ਬਿਖੈ ਕਰਵਤਿਹਿ ਪੈਹੌ। ਢੂੰਢਿ ਮੀਤ ਤੋ ਕੌ ਤਊ ਲੈਹੌ। ੨੮।","roman":"Kaasee bikhai karavtihi paihau | dhoondhi meet to kau taoo laihau | 28 |","meaning_en":"in Kashi I will put myself under the saw; even so, my friend, I will search you out.\"","page":1353,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਰਵਤ: the saw at Kashi under which devotees offered themselves.","meaning_pa":"ਕਾਸ਼ੀ ਵਿਚ ਆਰੇ ਨਾਲ ਚਿਰਵਾਵਾਗੀ। ਹੇ ਮਿੱਤਰ! ਤੈਨੂੰ ਤਦ (ਜਾ ਕੇ) ਲਭ ਲਵਾਗੀ ॥੨੮॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਅੜਿਲ","gurmukhi":"ਅੜਿਲ","roman":"Aril","meaning_en":"Arril.","page":1353,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅੜਿਲ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[29],"number_text":"੨੯।","page":1353,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਹਾ ਪਿਯਰਵਾ ਚਲੇ ਪ੍ਰਾਨ ਤਿਤਹੀ ਚਲੇ।","roman":"Jahaa piyarvaa chale praan tithee chale |","meaning_en":"Where my beloved goes, my life goes there too;","page":1353,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਿਥੇ ਪਿਆਰਾ ਚਲੇਗਾ, ਪ੍ਰਾਣ ਉਥੇ ਹੀ ਜਾਣਗੇ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਕਲ ਸਿਥਿਲ ਭਏ ਅੰਗ ਸੰਗ ਜੈਹੈ ਭਲੇ।","roman":"Sakal sithil bhae ang sang jaihai bhale |","meaning_en":"all my limbs have gone slack; it would be good to go with him.","page":1353,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸਾਰੇ ਅੰਗ ਸਿਥਲ ਹੋ ਗਏ ਹਨ, (ਪ੍ਰੀਤਮ) ਦੇ ਨਾਲ ਜਾਣਾ ਹੀ ਚੰਗਾ ਹੈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਾਧਵਨਲ ਕੌ ਨਾਮੁ ਮੰਤ੍ਰ ਸੋ ਜਾਨਿਯੈ।","roman":"Maadhavnal kau naamu mantr so jaaniyai |","meaning_en":"Know the name of Madhavanal as a mantra;","page":1353,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਮਾਧਵਾਨਲ ਦੇ ਨਾ ਨੂੰ ਮੰਤ੍ਰ ਸਮਝਣਾ ਚਾਹੀਦਾ ਹੈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹੋ ਜਾਤੌ ਲਗਤ ਉਚਾਟ ਸਤਿ ਕਰਿ ਮਾਨਿਯੈ। ੨੯।","roman":"Ho jaatau lagat uchaat sati kari maaniyai | 29 |","meaning_en":"as he goes, a restless anguish seizes me; take this as true.","page":1353,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਹੋ: metrical exclamation opening the last line of an arril; left untranslated. ਉਚਾਟ: restlessness, being uprooted (also a spell causing it).","meaning_pa":"(ਇਸ ਦੇ) ਲਗਣ ਨਾਲ ਉਦਾਸੀ ਚਲੀ ਜਾਦੀ ਹੈ। ਇਸ ਨੂੰ ਸਤਿ ਕਰ ਕੇ ਸਮਝੋ ॥੨੯॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":1353,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[30],"number_text":"੩੦।","page":1353,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੋ ਤੁਮਰੀ ਬਾਛਾ ਕਰਤ ਪ੍ਰਾਨ ਹਰੈ ਜਮ ਮੋਹਿ।","roman":"Jo tumree baachhaa karat praan harai jam mohi |","meaning_en":"If, while I am longing for you, Yama takes my life,","page":1353,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜੇ ਤੁਹਾਡੀ ਇੱਛਾ ਕਰਦਿਆਂ ਜਮ ਮੇਰੇ ਪ੍ਰਾਣ ਹਰ ਲਏ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਰੇ ਪਰਾਤ ਚੁਰੈਲ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਚਮਕਿ ਚਿਤੈਹੌ ਤੋਹਿ। ੩੦।","roman":"Mare paraat churail hvai chamki chitaihau tohi | 30 |","meaning_en":"after dying I will become a churail and gaze at you with a flash.","page":1353,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਚੁਰੈਲ: a female ghost. ਮਰੇ ਪਰਾਤ: read as 'after death'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਤਾ ਮੈਂ ਮਰਨ ਉਪਰੰਤ ਚੁੜੇਲ ਬਣ ਕੇ ਚਮਕ ਕੇ ਤੁਹਾਨੂੰ ਵੇਖਾਗੀ ॥੩੦॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[31],"number_text":"੩੧।","page":1353,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਰੀ ਬਿਰਹ ਕੀ ਆਗਿ ਮੈ ਜਰੀ ਰਖੈ ਹੌ ਨਾਉ।","roman":"Baree birah kee aagi mai jaree rakhai hau naau |","meaning_en":"Burnt in the fire of separation, I will keep the name 'the burnt one';","page":1353,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Wordplay on ਬਰੀ/ਜਰੀ ('burnt'); the line is obscure; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਬਿਰਹੋਂ ਦੀ ਅੱਗ ਵਿਚ ਸੜ ਕੇ ਮੈਂ ਆਪਣਾ ਨਾ ਜੜੀ-ਬੂਟੀ ਰਖ ਲਵਾਗੀ","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਾਤਿ ਜਰੀ ਕੀ ਬਰੀ ਕੀ ਢਿਗ ਤੇ ਕਬਹੂੰ ਨ ਜਾਉ। ੩੧।","roman":"Bhaati jaree kee baree kee dhig te kabhoon na jaau | 31 |","meaning_en":"like the jari and the bari, I will never go from your side.\"","page":1353,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਜਰੀ, ਬਰੀ: possibly two plants or items that grow or stay together; reading uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਅਤੇ ਜੜੀ-ਬੂਟੀ ਵਾਗ (ਪ੍ਰੀਤਮ ਦੇ) ਨੇੜਿਓਾਂ ਕਦੇ ਵੀ ਨਹੀਂ ਜਾਵਾਗੀ ॥੩੧॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[32],"number_text":"੩੨।","page":1353,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਾਚ ਕਹਤ ਹੈ ਬਿਰਹਨੀ ਰਹੀ ਪ੍ਰੇਮ ਸੌ ਪਾਗਿ।","roman":"Saach kahat hai birahnee rahee prem sau paagi |","meaning_en":"The woman in separation speaks the truth, steeped in love:","page":1353,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸਚ ਕਹਿੰਦੀ ਹਾ ਕਿ (ਮੈਂ) ਵਿਯੋਗਣ ਪ੍ਰੇਮ ਵਿਚ ਮਗਨ ਹੋ ਗਈ ਹਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਡਰਤ ਬਿਰਹ ਕੀ ਅਗਨਿ ਸੌ ਜਰਤ ਕਾਠ ਕੀ ਆਗਿ। ੩੨।","roman":"Darat birah kee agni sau jarat kaath kee aagi | 32 |","meaning_en":"the fire that burns wood is afraid of the fire of separation.","page":1353,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਵਿਯੋਗ ਦੀ ਅੱਗ ਤੋਂ ਡਰਦੀ ਹੋਈ ਕਾਠ ਦੀ ਅੱਗ ਵਿਚ ਸੜਦੀ ਹਾ ॥੩੨॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[33],"number_text":"੩੩।","page":1353,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਬ ਮਾਧਵਨਲ ਉਠਿ ਚਲਿਯੋ ਭਯੋ ਪਵਨ ਕੋ ਭੇਸ।","roman":"Tab maadhavnal uthi chaliyo bhayo pavan ko bhes |","meaning_en":"Then Madhavanal rose and went, swift as the wind;","page":1353,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਭਯੋ ਪਵਨ ਕੋ ਭੇਸ: literally 'took the form of the wind'.","meaning_pa":"ਤਦ ਮਾਧਵਾਨਲ ਪੌਣ ਦੀ ਤੇਜ਼ੀ ਨਾਲ ਉਠ ਕੇ ਚਲ ਪਿਆ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਸ ਧੁਨਿ ਸੁਨਿ ਸਿਰ ਧੁਨਿ ਗਯੋ ਬਿਕ੍ਰਮ ਜਹਾ ਨਰੇਸ। ੩੩।","roman":"Jas dhuni suni sir dhuni gayo bikram jahaa nares | 33 |","meaning_en":"hearing the sound of his fame, he went, shaking his head, to where King Vikram was.","page":1353,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਿਰ ਧੁਨਿ: 'shaking (or beating) his head', a wordplay on ਧੁਨਿ ('sound'); uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਕੰਨਾ ਨਾਲ ਯਸ਼ ਦੀ ਧੁਨ ਸੁਣ ਕੇ ਅਤੇ ਸਿਰ ਨੂੰ ਹਿਲਾ ਕੇ ਉਥੇ ਗਿਆ, ਜਿਥੇ ਬਿਕ੍ਰਮਾਜੀਤ ਰਾਜਾ ਸੀ ॥੩੩॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":1353,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੌਪਈ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[34],"number_text":"੩੪।","page":1353,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਿਕ੍ਰਮ ਜਹਾ ਨਿਤਿ ਚਲਿ ਆਵੈ। ਪੂਜਿ ਗੌਰਜਾ ਕੌ ਗ੍ਰਿਹ ਜਾਵੈ।","roman":"Bikram jahaa niti chali aavai | pooji gaurjaa kau grih jaavai |","meaning_en":"There was a place where Vikram came daily, worshipped Gaurja, and went home;","page":1353,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਿਥੇ ਬਿਕ੍ਰਮਾਜੀਤ ਰੋਜ਼ ਚਲ ਕੇ ਆਉਾਂਦਾ ਸੀ ਅਤੇ ਗੌਰਜਾ ਦੀ ਪੂਜਾ ਕਰ ਕੇ ਘਰ ਜਾਦਾ ਸੀ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮੰਦਿਰ ਊਚ ਧੁਜਾ ਫਹਰਾਹੀ। ਫਟਕਾਚਲ ਲਖਿ ਤਾਹਿ ਲਜਾਹੀ। ੩੪।","roman":"Mandir ooch dhujaa phahraahee | phatkaachal lakhi taahi lajaahee | 34 |","meaning_en":"the temple was high, its flags fluttered; seeing it, the crystal mountain felt ashamed.","page":1353,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਫਟਕਾਚਲ: the crystal mountain (Kailash).","meaning_pa":"ਮੰਦਿਰ ਉਤੇ ਉੱਚੇ ਝੰਡੇ ਫਹਰਾ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ। ਉਸ ਨੂੰ ਵੇਖ ਕੇ ਕੈਲਾਸ਼ ਪਰਬਤ ('ਫਟਕਾਚਲ') ਵੀ ਲਜਾਉਾਂਦਾ ਸੀ ॥੩੪॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":1355,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[35],"number_text":"੩੫।","page":1355,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਿਹੀ ਠੌਰਿ ਮਾਧਵ ਗਯੋ ਦੋਹਾ ਲਿਖ੍ਯੋ ਬਨਾਇ।","roman":"Tihee thauri maadhav gayo dohaa likhyo banaai |","meaning_en":"Madhav went to that very place and wrote a dohra there:","page":1355,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਸ ਥਾ ਤੇ ਮਾਧਵਾਨਲ ਗਿਆ ਅਤੇ ਵਿਚਾਰ ਪੂਰਵਕ ਇਕ ਦੋਹਰਾ ਲਿਖਿਆ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੌ ਬਿਕ੍ਰਮ ਇਹ ਬਾਚਿ ਹੈ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਹੋ ਮੋਰ ਉਪਾਇ। ੩੫।","roman":"Jau bikram ih baachi hai hvai ho mor upaai | 35 |","meaning_en":"\"If Vikram reads this, my remedy will be found.","page":1355,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜੇ ਬਿਕ੍ਰਮਾਜੀਤ ਇਸ ਨੂੰ ਪੜ੍ਰਹੇਗਾ ਤਾ ਮੇਰਾ ਉਪਾ ਹੋਵੇਗਾ ॥੩੫॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[36],"number_text":"੩੬।","page":1355,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੇ ਨਰ ਰੋਗਨ ਸੌ ਗ੍ਰਸੇ ਤਿਨ ਕੋ ਹੋਤ ਉਪਾਉ।","roman":"Je nar rogan sau grase tin ko hot upaau |","meaning_en":"Men seized by diseases have a cure;","page":1355,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜੋ ਵਿਅਕਤੀ ਰੋਗਾ ਨਾਲ ਗ੍ਰਸਿਆ ਹੋਵੇ, ਉਸ ਦਾ ਉਪਾ ਹੋ ਜਾਦਾ ਹੈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਿਰਹ ਤ੍ਰਿਦੋਖਨ ਜੇ ਗ੍ਰਸੇ ਤਿਨ ਕੋ ਕਛੁ ਨ ਬਚਾਉ। ੩੬।","roman":"Birah tridokhan je grase tin ko kachhu na bachaau | 36 |","meaning_en":"those seized by separation, as by the disorder of the three humours, have no saving.\"","page":1355,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਤ੍ਰਿਦੋਖ: disorder of all three bodily humours, held to be incurable.","meaning_pa":"ਜੋ ਵਿਯੋਗ ਦੇ ਤ੍ਰੈ ਦੋਸ਼ਾ (ਹਡ, ਚੰਮ ਅਤੇ ਸੁਆਸ) ਦਾ ਗ੍ਰਸਿਆ ਹੋਵੇ, ਉਸ ਦਾ ਕੋਈ ਬਚਾ ਨਹੀਂ ਹੋ ਸਕਦਾ ॥੩੬॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":1355,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੌਪਈ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[37],"number_text":"੩੭।","page":1355,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਿਕ੍ਰਮ ਸੈਨਿ ਤਹਾ ਚਲਿ ਆਯੋ। ਆਨ ਗੌਰਜਾ ਕੌ ਸਿਰ ਨ੍ਯਾਯੋ।","roman":"Bikram saini tahaa chali aayo | aan gaurjaa kau sir nyaayo |","meaning_en":"Vikram Sen came there and bowed his head to Gaurja.","page":1355,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਰਾਜਾ ਬਿਕ੍ਰਮਾਜੀਤ ਉਥੇ ਚਲ ਕੇ ਆਇਆ। ਆ ਕੇ ਗੌਰਜਾ ਨੂੰ ਸਿਰ ਨਿਵਾਇਆ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਚਿ ਦੋਹਰਾ ਕੋ ਚਕਿ ਰਹਿਯੋ। ਕੋ ਬਿਰਹੀ ਆਯੋ ਹ੍ਯਾ ਕਹਿਯੋ। ੩੭।","roman":"Baachi dohraa ko chaki rahiyo | ko birhee aayo hyaa kahiyo | 37 |","meaning_en":"Reading the dohra he was astonished, and said, \"What lover in separation has come here?","page":1355,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਦੋਹਰਾ ਪੜ੍ਰਹ ਕੇ ਹੈਰਾਨ ਹੋ ਗਿਆ ਅਤੇ ਕਹਿਣ ਲਗਾ ਕੀ ਕੋਈ ਵਿਯੋਗੀ ਇਥੇ ਆਇਆ ਹੈ ॥੩੭॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":1355,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[38],"number_text":"੩੮।","page":1355,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕੋ ਬਿਰਹੀ ਆਯੋ ਹ੍ਯਾ ਤਾ ਕੌ ਲੇਹੁ ਬੁਲਾਇ।","roman":"Ko birhee aayo hyaa taa kau lehu bulaai |","meaning_en":"Whatever lover in separation has come here, call him to me;","page":1355,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੋ ਵਹੁ ਕਹੈ ਸੋ ਹੌ ਕਰੌ ਤਾ ਕੌ ਜਿਯਨ ਉਪਾਇ। ੩੮।","roman":"Jo vahu kahai so hau karau taa kau jiyan upaai | 38 |","meaning_en":"whatever he says I will do, as the means of saving his life.\"","page":1355,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਜੇ) ਕੋਈ ਵਿਯੋਗੀ ਇਥੇ ਆਇਆ ਹੈ, ਉਸ ਨੂੰ ਬੁਲਾ ਲਵੋ। ਉਸ ਦੇ ਜੀਣ ਦਾ ਜੋ ਉਪਾ ਉਹ ਕਹੇਗਾ, ਮੈਂ ਕਰਾਗਾ ॥੩੮॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB","note_pa":"ਇਹ ਅਰਥ ਇਸ ਪੰਕਤੀ ਸਮੇਤ ਉੱਪਰਲੀਆਂ 2 ਪੰਕਤੀਆਂ ਦਾ ਇਕੱਠਾ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":1355,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੌਪਈ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[39],"number_text":"੩੯।","page":1355,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਿਕ੍ਰਮ ਮਾਧਵ ਬੋਲਿ ਪਠਾਯੋ। ਆਦਰੁ ਦੈ ਆਸਨੁ ਬੈਠਾਯੋ।","roman":"Bikram maadhav boli pathaayo | aadru dai aasnu baithaayo |","meaning_en":"Vikram sent for Madhav, and with respect gave him a seat.","page":1355,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਬਿਕ੍ਰਮਾਜੀਤ ਨੇ ਮਾਧਵਾਨਲ ਨੂੰ ਬੁਲਾ ਭੇਜਿਆ। ਆਦਰ ਪੂਰਵਕ ਆਸਣ ਉਤੇ ਬਿਠਾਇਆ","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹਸਿ ਦਿਜਾਗ੍ਯਾ ਦੇਹੁ ਸੁ ਕਰਿਹੌ। ਪ੍ਰਾਨਨ ਲਗੇ ਹੇਤੁ ਤੁਹਿ ਲਰਿਹੋ। ੩੯।","roman":"Kahsi dijaagyaa dehu su karihau | praanan lage hetu tuhi lariho | 39 |","meaning_en":"He said, \"Brahmin, give your command and I will do it; for your sake I will fight with all my life.\"","page":1355,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਦਿਜਾਗ੍ਯਾ: ਦਿਜ ('brahmin') + ਆਗ੍ਯਾ ('command').","meaning_pa":"ਅਤੇ ਕਿਹਾ ਹੇ ਬ੍ਰਾਹਮਣ! ਜੋ ਆਗਿਆ ਦਿਓ, ਉਹੀ ਕਰਾਗਾ। ਜੇ ਪ੍ਰਾਣ ਵੀ ਲਗ ਜਾਣ ਤਾ ਵੀ ਤੇਰੇ ਲਈ ਲੜਾਗਾ ॥੩੯॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[40],"number_text":"੪੦।","page":1355,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਬ ਮਾਧਵ ਕਹਿ ਭੇਦ ਸੁਨਾਯੋ। ਤਬ ਬਿਕ੍ਰਮ ਸਭ ਸੈਨ ਬੁਲਾਯੋ।","roman":"Jab maadhav kahi bhed sunaayo | tab bikram sabh sain bulaayo |","meaning_en":"When Madhav told him the secret, Vikram called up all his army.","page":1355,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਦ ਮਾਧਵਾਨਲ ਨੇ ਭੇਦ ਦਸਿਆ, ਤਾ ਬਿਕ੍ਰਮਜੀਤ ਨੇ ਸਾਰੀ ਸੈਨਾ ਬੁਲਾ ਲਈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਾਜੇ ਸਸਤ੍ਰ ਕੌਚ ਤਨ ਧਾਰੇ। ਕਾਮਵਤੀ ਕੀ ਓਰ ਸਿਧਾਰੇ। ੪੦।","roman":"Saaje sasatr kauch tan dhaare | kaamavtee kee or sidhaare | 40 |","meaning_en":"They fitted on their weapons, put armour on their bodies, and set out toward Kamavati.","page":1355,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸ਼ਸਤ੍ਰ ਧਾਰ ਲਏ ਅਤੇ (ਸ਼ਰੀਰ ਉਤੇ) ਕਵਚ ਪਾ ਲਏ ਅਤੇ ਕਾਮਵਤੀ ਨਗਰੀ ਵਲ ਤੁਰ ਪਏ ॥੪੦॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸੋਰਠਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸੋਰਠਾ","roman":"Sorthaa","meaning_en":"Sortha.","page":1355,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸੋਰਠਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[41],"number_text":"੪੧।","page":1355,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਦੂਤ ਪਠਾਯੋ ਏਕ ਕਾਮਸੈਨ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਸੌ ਕਹੈ।","roman":"Doot pathaayo ek kaamsain nrip sau kahai |","meaning_en":"He sent an envoy to say to King Kam Sen:","page":1355,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਉਸ ਨੇ) ਇਕ ਦੂਤ ਭੇਜਿਆ ਕਿ ਕਾਮਸੈਨ ਰਾਜੇ ਨੂੰ ਕਹੇ","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਮਕੰਦਲਾ ਏਕ ਦੈ ਸਭ ਦੇਸ ਉਬਾਰਿਯੈ। ੪੧।","roman":"Kaamkandlaa ek dai sabh des ubaariyai | 41 |","meaning_en":"\"Give up Kamakandla alone, and save the whole country.\"","page":1355,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਿ ਇਕ ਕਾਮਕੰਦਲਾ ਦੇ ਕੇ ਆਪਣੇ ਦੇਸ਼ ਨੂੰ ਬਚਾ ਲਏ ॥੪੧॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":1355,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੌਪਈ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[42],"number_text":"੪੨।","page":1355,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਮਵਤੀ ਭੀਤਰ ਦੂਤਾਯੋ। ਕਾਮਸੈਨ ਜੂ ਕੋ ਸਿਰੁ ਨ੍ਯਾਯੋ।","roman":"Kaamavtee bheetar dootaayo | kaamsain joo ko siru nyaayo |","meaning_en":"The envoy came into Kamavati and bowed his head to Kam Sen.","page":1355,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਦੂਤਾਯੋ: printed so; read as ਦੂਤ ਆਯੋ, 'the envoy came'.","meaning_pa":"ਕਾਮਵਤੀ ਨਗਰੀ ਵਿਚ ਦੂਤ ਆਇਆ। (ਉਸ ਨੇ ਆ ਕੇ) ਕਾਮਸੈਨ ਨੂੰ ਸਿਰ ਨਿਵਾਇਆ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਿਕ੍ਰਮ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਸੁ ਤਾਹਿ ਸੁਨਾਵਾ। ਅਧਿਕ ਰਾਵ ਕੋ ਦੁਖ ਉਪਜਾਵਾ। ੪੨।","roman":"Bikram kahiyo su taahi sunaavaa | adhik raav ko dukh upjaavaa | 42 |","meaning_en":"He told him what Vikram had said, and caused the king great distress.","page":1355,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਜੋ) ਬਿਕ੍ਰਮ ਨੇ ਕਿਹਾ ਸੀ, ਉਹ ਉਸ ਨੂੰ ਸੁਣਾ ਦਿੱਤਾ। (ਇਸ ਤਰ੍ਰਹਾ) ਰਾਜੇ ਨੂੰ ਬਹੁਤ ਦੁਖ ਹੋਇਆ ॥੪੨॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":1355,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[43],"number_text":"੪੩।","page":1355,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਿਸਿਸਿ ਚੜੇ ਦਿਨ ਕੇ ਭਏ ਨਿਸਿ ਰਵਿ ਕਰੈ ਉਦੋਤ।","roman":"Nisisi chare din ke bhae nisi ravi karai udot |","meaning_en":"\"Even if the moon rises by day and the sun shines at night,","page":1355,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਨਿਸਿਸਿ: the moon (lord of night).","meaning_pa":"(ਰਾਜੇ ਨੇ ਮਨ ਵਿਚ ਵਿਚਾਰਿਆ) ਦਿਨ ਦੇ ਹੁੰਦਿਆਂ ਚੰਨ ਭਾਵੇ ਚੜ੍ਰਹੇ ਅਤੇ ਰਾਤ ਨੂੰ ਸੂਰਜ ਚੜ੍ਰਹ ਪਏ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਮਕੰਦਲਾ ਕੋ ਦਿਯਬ ਤਊ ਨ ਹਮ ਤੇ ਹੋਤ। ੪੩।","roman":"Kaamkandlaa ko diyab taoo na ham te hot | 43 |","meaning_en":"still I will not give up Kamakandla.\"","page":1355,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤਾ ਵੀ ਕਾਮਕੰਦਲਾ ਨੂੰ ਦੇਣਾ ਮੇਰੇ ਪਾਸੋਂ (ਸੰਭਵ) ਨਹੀਂ ਹੋਣਾ ॥੪੩॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਦੂਤੋ ਬਾਚ","gurmukhi":"ਦੂਤੋ ਬਾਚ","roman":"Dooto baach","meaning_en":"The envoy said:","page":1355,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੂਤ ਨੇ ਕਿਹਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਭੁਜੰਗ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਭੁਜੰਗ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Bhujang chhand","meaning_en":"Bhujang metre.","page":1355,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਭੁਜੰਗ ਛੰਦ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[44],"number_text":"੪੪।","page":1355,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਨੋ ਰਾਜ ਕਹਾ ਨਾਰਿ ਕਾਮਾ ਬਿਚਾਰੀ। ਕਹਾ ਗਾਠਿ ਬਾਧੀ ਤੁਮੈ ਜਾਨਿ ਪ੍ਯਾਰੀ।","roman":"Suno raaj kahaa naari kaamaa bichaaree | kahaa gaathi baadhee tumai jaani pyaaree |","meaning_en":"\"Listen, king: what is this poor woman Kama? Why have you tied her into your knot, thinking her dear?","page":1355,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹੇ ਰਾਜਨ! ਸੁਣੋ, ਇਹ ਕਾਮਕੰਦਲਾ ਨਾਰੀ ਵਿਚਾਰੀ ਕੀ ਹੈ। (ਇਸ ਨੂੰ) ਤੁਸੀਂ ਕਿਉਾਂ ਗੰਢ ਬੰਨ੍ਰਹ ਕੇ ਜਾਨ ਤੋਂ ਪਿਆਰੀ ਕਰ ਕੇ ਰਖਿਆ ਹੈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹੀ ਮਾਨਿ ਮੇਰੀ ਕਹਾ ਨਾਹਿ ਭਾਖੋ। ਇਨੈ ਦੈ ਮਿਲੌ ਤਾਹਿ ਕੌ ਗਰਬ ਰਾਖੋ। ੪੪।","roman":"Kahee maani meree kahaa naahi bhaakho | inai dai milau taahi kau garab raakho | 44 |","meaning_en":"Heed what I say; why do you say no? Give her up, meet him, and keep your pride.","page":1355,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਤਾਹਿ ਕੌ ਗਰਬ ਰਾਖੋ: possibly 'respect his pride'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਮੇਰਾ ਕਿਹਾ ਮੰਨੋ, (ਜੋ ਮੈਨੂੰ) ਰਾਜੇ ਨੇ ਕਿਹਾ ਹੈ, ਉਹੀ ਕਹਿ ਰਿਹਾ ਹਾ। ਇਸ ਨੂੰ ਦੇ ਕੇ (ਰਾਜੇ ਨੂੰ ਮਿਲੋ) ਅਤੇ ਉਸ ਦਾ ਮਾਣ ਰਖ ਲਵੋ ॥੪੪॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":1357,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Printed heading Chaupai, though the verses that follow are in the Bhujang metre.","meaning_pa":"ਚੌਪਈ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[45],"number_text":"੪੫।","page":1357,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਹਠੀ ਹੈ ਹਮਾਰੀ ਸੁ ਤੁਮਹੂੰ ਪਛਾਨੋ। ਦਿਸਾ ਚਾਰਿ ਜਾ ਕੀ ਸਦਾ ਲੋਹ ਮਾਨੋ।","roman":"Hathee hai hamaaree su tumhoon pachhaano | disaa chaari jaa kee sadaa loh maano |","meaning_en":"Our king is resolute, as you yourself know; his steel is acknowledged in all four directions.","page":1357,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਲੀ ਦੇਵ ਆਦੇਵ ਜਾ ਕੌ ਬਖਾਨੈ। ਕਹਾ ਰੋਕ ਤੂ ਤੌਨ ਸੋ ਜੁਧੁ ਠਾਨੈ। ੪੫।","roman":"Balee dev aadev jaa kau bakhaanai | kahaa rok too taun so judhu thaanai | 45 |","meaning_en":"Gods and demons call him mighty; what are you, that you would make war with him?\"","page":1357,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਹਾ ਰੋਕ ਤੂ: read as 'what hindrance are you'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[46],"number_text":"੪੬।","page":1357,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਜੀ ਦੁੰਦਭੀ ਦੀਹ ਦਰਬਾਰ ਭਾਰੇ। ਜਬੈ ਦੂਤ ਕਟੁ ਬੈਨ ਐਸੇ ਉਚਾਰੇ।","roman":"Bajee dundbhee deeh darbaar bhaare | jabai doot katu bain aise uchaare |","meaning_en":"Great kettle-drums sounded in the mighty court when the envoy uttered such bitter words.","page":1357,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹਠਿਯੋ ਬੀਰ ਹਾਠੌ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਜੁਧ ਮੰਡੋ। ਕਹਾ ਬਿਕ੍ਰਮਾ ਕਾਲ ਕੋ ਖੰਡ ਖੰਡੋ। ੪੬।","roman":"Hathiyo beer haathau kahiyo judh mando | kahaa bikramaa kaal ko khand khando | 46 |","meaning_en":"The stubborn warrior said obstinately, \"Make war! What is Vikram? I would cut Death itself to pieces.\"","page":1357,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Speaker taken as Kam Sen; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[47],"number_text":"੪੭।","page":1357,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਚੜਿਯੋ ਲੈ ਅਨੀ ਕੋ ਬਲੀ ਬੀਰ ਭਾਰੇ। ਖੰਡੇਲੇ ਬਘੇਲੇ ਪੰਧੇਰੇ ਪਵਾਰੇ।","roman":"Chariyo lai anee ko balee beer bhaare | khandele baghele pandhere pavaare |","meaning_en":"He rode out with his army of mighty, great warriors: Khandele, Baghele, Pandhere, Panwar;","page":1357,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Rajput clan names."},{"gurmukhi":"ਗਹਰਵਾਰ ਚੌਹਾਨ ਗਹਲੌਤ ਦੌਰੈ। ਮਹਾ ਜੰਗ ਜੋਧਾ ਜਿਤੇ ਨਾਹਿ ਔਰੈ। ੪੭।","roman":"Gaharvaar chauhaan gahlaut daurai | mahaa jang jodhaa jite naahi aurai | 47 |","meaning_en":"Gaharwar, Chauhan and Gahlot rushed on, great warriors whom no others could defeat.","page":1357,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Rajput clan names."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[48],"number_text":"੪੮।","page":1357,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਨ੍ਯੋ ਬਿਕ੍ਰਮਾ ਬੀਰ ਸਭ ਹੀ ਬੁਲਾਏ। ਠਟੇ ਠਾਟ ਗਾੜੇ ਚਲੇ ਖੇਤ ਆਏ।","roman":"Sunyo bikramaa beer sabh hee bulaae | thate thaat gaare chale khet aae |","meaning_en":"Vikram heard and summoned all his warriors; they formed in dense array and came onto the field.","page":1357,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਦੁਹੂੰ ਉਰ ਤੇ ਸੂਰ ਸੈਨਾ ਉਮੰਗੈ। ਮਿਲੇ ਜਾਇ ਜਮੁਨਾ ਮਨੌ ਧਾਇ ਗੰਗੈ। ੪੮।","roman":"Duhoon ur te soor sainaa umangai | mile jaai jamunaa manau dhaai gangai | 48 |","meaning_en":"From both sides the armies of heroes surged forward, as if the Jamuna rushed to meet the Ganga.","page":1357,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[49],"number_text":"੪੯।","page":1357,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿਤੇ ਬੀਰ ਕਰਵਾਰਿ ਕਾਢੈ ਚਲਾਵੈ। ਕਿਤੇ ਚਰਮ ਪੈ ਘਾਇ ਤਾ ਕੋ ਬਚਾਵੈ।","roman":"Kite beer karvaari kaadhai chalaavai | kite charam pai ghaai taa ko bachaavai |","meaning_en":"Some warriors draw their swords and wield them; some guard against the blows on their shields;","page":1357,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿਤੋ ਬਰਮ ਪੈ ਚਰਮ ਰੁਪਿ ਗਰਮ ਝਾਰੈ। ਉਠੈ ਨਾਦ ਭਾਰੇ ਛੁਟੈ ਚਿੰਨਗਾਰੈ। ੪੯।","roman":"Kito baram pai charam rupi garam jhaarai | uthai naad bhaare chhutai chinngaarai | 49 |","meaning_en":"some, holding firm with shield and armour, strike fierce blows; great clangs rise and sparks fly.","page":1357,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਰੁਪਿ ਗਰਮ ਝਾਰੈ: read as 'standing firm, strike hot blows'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[50],"number_text":"੫੦।","page":1357,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿਤੇ ਗੋਫਨੈ ਗੁਰਜ ਗੋਲਾ ਚਲਾਵੈ। ਕਿਤੇ ਅਰਧ ਚੰਦ੍ਰਾਦਿ ਬਾਨਾ ਬਜਾਵੈ।","roman":"Kite gophnai guraj golaa chalaavai | kite aradh chandraadi baanaa bajaavai |","meaning_en":"Some hurl with slings, maces and iron balls; some shoot crescent-headed and other arrows;","page":1357,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿਤੇ ਸੂਲ ਸੈਥੀ ਸੂਆ ਹਾਥ ਲੈ ਕੈ। ਮੰਡੇ ਆਨਿ ਜੋਧਾ ਮਹਾ ਕੋਪ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਕੈ। ੫੦।","roman":"Kite sool saithee sooaa haath lai kai | mande aani jodhaa mahaa kop hvai kai | 50 |","meaning_en":"some, taking tridents, lances and spears in hand, close in combat, the warriors in great fury.","page":1357,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[51],"number_text":"੫੧।","page":1357,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਫਰੀ ਧੋਪ ਖਾਂਡੇ ਲਏ ਫਾਸ ਐਸੀ। ਮਨੌ ਨਾਰਿ ਕੇ ਸਾਹੁ ਕੀ ਜੁਲਫ ਜੈਸੀ।","roman":"Pharee dhop khaande lae phaas aisee | manau naari ke saahu kee julaph jaisee |","meaning_en":"With shields, broadswords and double-edged swords, they took up nooses like the curling locks of a lover;","page":1357,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਨਾਰਿ ਕੇ ਸਾਹੁ ਕੀ ਜੁਲਫ: literally 'the locks of a woman's lord'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਰੀ ਮਤ ਕੀ ਭਾਤਿ ਮਾਰਤ ਬਿਹਾਰੈ। ਜਿਸੇ ਕੰਠਿ ਡਾਰੈ ਤਿਸੈ ਐਚ ਮਾਰੈ। ੫੧।","roman":"Karee mat kee bhaati maarat bihaarai | jise kanthi daarai tisai aich maarai | 51 |","meaning_en":"like maddened elephants they range about killing; whomever they throw it round the neck of, they drag and kill.","page":1357,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[52],"number_text":"੫੨।","page":1357,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਬ ਇਹ ਭਾਤਿ ਸਕਲ ਭਟ ਲਰੇ। ਟੂਕ ਟੂਕ ਰਨ ਮੈ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਪਰੇ।","roman":"Jab ih bhaati sakal bhat lare | took took ran mai hvai pare |","meaning_en":"When all the warriors had fought in this way and lay in pieces on the battlefield,","page":1357,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਦ ਇਸ ਤਰ੍ਰਹਾ ਸਾਰੇ ਯੋਧੇ ਲੜੇ ਅਤੇ ਟੋਟੇ ਟੋਟੇ ਹੋ ਕੇ ਯੁੱਧ-ਭੂਮੀ ਵਿਚ ਡਿਗ ਪਏ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਬ ਬਿਕ੍ਰਮ ਹਸਿ ਬੈਨ ਉਚਾਰੋ। ਕਾਮਸੈਨ ਸੁਨੁ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਹਮਾਰੋ। ੫੨।","roman":"Tab bikram hasi bain uchaaro | kaamsain sunu kahiyo hamaaro | 52 |","meaning_en":"then Vikram laughed and spoke: \"Kam Sen, listen to what I say.","page":1357,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤਦ ਬਿਕ੍ਰਮ ਨੇ ਹਸ ਕੇ ਕਿਹਾ, ਹੇ ਕਾਮਸੈਨ! ਸਾਡੀ ਕਹੀ ਗੱਲ ਸੁਣ ॥੫੨॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":1357,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[53],"number_text":"੫੩।","page":1357,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਦੈ ਬੇਸ੍ਵਾ ਇਹ ਬਿਪ੍ਰ ਕੌ ਸੁਨੁ ਰੇ ਬਚਨ ਅਚੇਤ।","roman":"Dai besvaa ih bipr kau sunu re bachan achet |","meaning_en":"Give this courtesan to the brahmin; listen to my words, you senseless one.","page":1357,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹੇ ਮੂਰਖ! ਗੱਲ ਸੁਣੋ, ਇਸ ਬ੍ਰਾਹਮਣ ਨੂੰ ਇਹ ਵੇਸਵਾ ਦੇ ਦਿਓ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬ੍ਰਿਥਾ ਜੁਝਾਰਤ ਕ੍ਯੋ ਕਟਕ ਏਕ ਨਟੀ ਕੇ ਹੇਤ। ੫੩।","roman":"Brithaa jujhaarat kyo katak ek natee ke het | 53 |","meaning_en":"Why have the army slain for nothing, for the sake of one dancing-girl?\"","page":1357,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਇਕ ਨਾਚੀ ਲਈ ਵਿਅਰਥ ਵਿਚ ਸੈਨਾ ਨੂੰ ਕਿਉਾਂ ਮਰਵਾ ਰਹੇ ਹੋ ॥੫੩॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":1357,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੌਪਈ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[54],"number_text":"੫੪।","page":1357,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਮਸੈਨ ਤਿਹ ਕਹੀ ਨ ਕਰੀ। ਪੁਨਿ ਬਿਕ੍ਰਮ ਹਸਿ ਯਹੈ ਉਚਰੀ।","roman":"Kaamsain tih kahee na karee | puni bikram hasi yahai uchree |","meaning_en":"Kam Sen did not do as he said; again Vikram laughed and said this:","page":1357,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਾਮਸੈਨ ਨੇ ਉਸ ਦੀ ਕਹੀ ਗੱਲ ਨੂੰ ਨਾ ਮੰਨਿਆ। ਬਿਕ੍ਰਮ ਨੇ ਫਿਰ ਹਸ ਕੇ ਇਹੀ ਕਿਹਾ","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹਮ ਤੁਮ ਲਰੈ ਕਪਟ ਤਜਿ ਦੋਈ। ਕੈ ਜੀਤੇ ਕੈ ਹਾਰੈ ਕੋਈ। ੫੪।","roman":"Ham tum larai kapat taji doee | kai jeete kai haarai koee | 54 |","meaning_en":"\"Let us two fight, you and I, without deceit; either one shall win or one shall lose.","page":1357,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਿ ਅਸੀਂ ਅਤੇ ਤੁਸੀਂ ਦੋਵੇਾਂ ਕਪਟ ਛਡ ਕੇ ਲੜੀਏ, ਭਾਵੇਾਂ ਕੋਈ ਜਿੱਤੇ ਭਾਵੇਾਂ ਹਾਰੇ ॥੫੪॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[55],"number_text":"੫੫।","page":1357,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਪਨੀ ਅਪਨੇ ਹੀ ਸਿਰ ਲੀਜੈ। ਔਰਨ ਕੇ ਸਿਰ ਬ੍ਰਿਥਾ ਨ ਦੀਜੈ।","roman":"Apnee apne hee sir leejai | auran ke sir brithaa na deejai |","meaning_en":"Let each take his own quarrel on his own head, and not lay it needlessly on the heads of others.","page":1357,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਆਪਣੀ ਲੜਾਈ ਆਪਣੇ ਹੀ ਸਿਰ ਉਤੇ ਲਈਏ ਅਤੇ ਹੋਰਨਾ ਦੇ ਸਿਰ ਉਤੇ ਵਿਅਰਥ ਵਿਚ ਨਾ ਮੜ੍ਰਹੀਏ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬੈਠਿ ਬਿਗਾਰਿ ਆਪੁ ਜੋ ਕਰਿਯੈ। ਨਾਹਕ ਔਰ ਲੋਕ ਨਹਿ ਮਰਿਯੈ। ੫੫।","roman":"Baithi bigaari aapu jo kariyai | naahak aur lok nahi mariyai | 55 |","meaning_en":"If one has made the trouble oneself, other people should not die for nothing.\"","page":1357,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਅਸੀਂ) ਆਪ ਬੈਠ ਕੇ ਜੋ ਵਿਗਾੜ ਕਰਦੇ ਹਾ, ਉਸ ਵਿਚ ਨਾਹਕ ਹੋਰਾ ਲੋਕਾ ਨੂੰ ਨਾ ਮਰਵਾਈਏ ॥੫੫॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":1359,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[56],"number_text":"੫੬।","page":1359,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਮਸੈਨ ਇਹ ਬਚਨ ਸੁਨਿ ਅਧਿਕ ਉਠਿਯੋ ਰਿਸ ਖਾਇ।","roman":"Kaamsain ih bachan suni adhik uthiyo ris khaai |","meaning_en":"Hearing these words, Kam Sen rose up in great anger;","page":1359,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਾਮਸੈਨ ਇਹ ਗੱਲ ਸੁਣ ਕੇ ਬਹੁਤ ਕ੍ਰੋਧਵਾਨ ਹੋ ਕੇ ਉਠਿਆ","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਪਨੌ ਤੁਰੈ ਧਵਾਇ ਕੈ ਬਿਕ੍ਰਮ ਲਯੋ ਬੁਲਾਇ। ੫੬।","roman":"Apnau turai dhavaai kai bikram layo bulaai | 56 |","meaning_en":"spurring his horse forward, he challenged Vikram.","page":1359,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅਤੇ ਆਪਣੇ ਘੋੜੇ ਨੂੰ ਦੌੜਾ ਕੇ ਬਿਕ੍ਰਮ ਨੂੰ ਬੁਲਾ ਲਿਆ ॥੫੬॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[57],"number_text":"੫੭।","page":1359,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਮਸੈਨ ਐਸੇ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਸੂਰ ਸਾਮੁਹੇ ਜਾਇ।","roman":"Kaamsain aise kahiyo soor saamuhe jaai |","meaning_en":"Going face to face with the hero, Kam Sen said this:","page":1359,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਾਮਸੈਨ ਨੇ (ਉਸ) ਸੂਰਮੇ ਦੇ ਸਾਹਮਣੇ ਜਾ ਕੇ ਕਿਹਾ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਝਾਗਿ ਸੈਹਥੀ ਬ੍ਰਿਣ ਕਰੈ ਤੌ ਤੂ ਬਿਕ੍ਰਮ ਸਰਾਇ। ੫੭।","roman":"Jhaagi saihthee brin karai tau too bikram saraai | 57 |","meaning_en":"\"If you can bear the thrust of a lance and the wound it makes, then, Vikram, you are worthy of praise.\"","page":1359,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਰਾਇ: read as 'praiseworthy'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਤੂੰ ਮੇਰੀ ਸੈਹਥੀ ਦਾ ਵਾਰ ਸਹਾਰ ਕੇ (ਜੇ ਫਿਰ ਮੈਨੂੰ) ਘਾਇਲ ਕਰ ਦੇਏਾਂ, ਤਾ ਹੀ ਤੂੰ ਬਿਕ੍ਰਮ ਰਾਜਾ (ਸਮਝਿਆ ਜਾਵੇਾਂਗਾ) ॥੫੭॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[58],"number_text":"੫੮।","page":1359,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਝਾਗਿ ਸੈਹਥੀ ਪੇਟ ਮਹਿ ਚਿਤ ਮਹਿ ਅਧਿਕ ਰਿਸਾਇ।","roman":"Jhaagi saihthee pet mahi chit mahi adhik risaai |","meaning_en":"Taking the lance in his belly, and greatly enraged at heart,","page":1359,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਰਾਜਾ ਕਾਮਸੈਨ ਵਲੋਂ ਕੀਤੇ) ਸੈਹਥੀ ਦੇ ਵਾਰ ਨੂੰ ਪੇਟ ਵਿਚ ਸਹਾਰ ਕੇ ਅਤੇ ਮਨ ਵਿਚ ਬਹੁਤ ਕ੍ਰੋਧਵਾਨ ਹੋ ਕੇ","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਆਨਿ ਕਟਾਰੀ ਕੋ ਕਿਯੋ ਕਾਮਸੈਨ ਕੋ ਘਾਇ। ੫੮।","roman":"Aani kataaree ko kiyo kaamsain ko ghaai | 58 |","meaning_en":"he came on and struck Kam Sen with a dagger.","page":1359,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਾਮਸੈਨ ਨੂੰ ਕਟਾਰ ਨਾਲ ਘਾਇਲ ਕਰ ਦਿੱਤਾ ॥੫੮॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[59],"number_text":"੫੯।","page":1359,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਐਸੇ ਕੌ ਐਸੋ ਲਹਤ ਜਿਯਤ ਨ ਛਾਡਤ ਔਰ।","roman":"Aise kau aiso lahat jiyat na chhaadat aur |","meaning_en":"Such a one finds such a match; he does not leave the other alive.","page":1359,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅਜਿਹੇ ਨੂੰ ਅਜਿਹਾ ਹੀ ਟਕਰਨਾ ਚਾਹੀਦਾ ਹੈ ਅਤੇ (ਉਸ ਨੂੰ) ਜੀਉਾਂਦਾ ਨਹੀਂ ਛਡਣਾ ਚਾਹੀਦਾ ਹੈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਾਰਿ ਕਟਾਰੀ ਰਾਖਿਯੋ ਜਿਯਤ ਰਾਵ ਤਿਹ ਠੌਰ। ੫੯।","roman":"Maari kataaree raakhiyo jiyat raav tih thaur | 59 |","meaning_en":"Striking with the dagger, he kept the king alive in that place.","page":1359,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Translated as printed; the line seems to contrast with the first half, and the sense is unclear (perhaps Vikram, though struck, stayed alive, or the wound was not fatal at once).","meaning_pa":"(ਉਸ ਨੇ) ਕਟਾਰ ਮਾਰ ਕੇ ਜੀਉਾਂਦੇ ਰਾਜੇ ਨੂੰ ਉਸ ਸਥਾਨ ਉਤੇ ਟਿਕਾ ਦਿੱਤਾ ॥੫੯॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":1359,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੌਪਈ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[60],"number_text":"੬੦।","page":1359,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੀਤਿ ਤਾਹਿ ਸਭ ਸੈਨ ਬੁਲਾਈ। ਭਾਤਿ ਭਾਤਿ ਕੀ ਬਜੀ ਬਧਾਈ।","roman":"Jeeti taahi sabh sain bulaaee | bhaati bhaati kee bajee badhaaee |","meaning_en":"Having conquered him, he called together all his army; congratulations sounded in many ways.","page":1359,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਸ ਨੂੰ ਜਿਤ ਕੇ (ਬਿਕ੍ਰਮ ਨੇ) ਸਾਰੀ ਸੈਨਾ ਬੁਲਾ ਲਈ। ਭਾਤ ਭਾਤ ਦੇ ਵਧਾਵੇ ਵਜਣ ਲਗੇ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਦੇਵਨ ਰੀਝਿ ਇਹੈ ਬਰੁ ਦਯੋ। ਬ੍ਰਣੀ ਹੁਤੋ ਅਬ੍ਰਣ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਗਯੋ। ੬੦।","roman":"Devan reejhi ihai baru dayo | branee huto abran hvai gayo | 60 |","meaning_en":"The gods, pleased, gave this boon: he who was wounded became unwounded.","page":1359,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੇਵਤਿਆਂ ਨੇ ਪ੍ਰਸੰਨ ਹੋ ਕੇ ਇਹ ਵਰ ਦਿੱਤਾ (ਜਿਸ ਕਰ ਕੇ) ਘਾਇਲ (ਰਾਜਾ ਬਿਕ੍ਰਮ) ਦੇ ਜ਼ਖ਼ਮ ਠੀਕ ਹੋ ਗਏ ॥੬੦॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":1359,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[61],"number_text":"੬੧।","page":1359,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਥਿਤ ਭੇਖ ਸਜਿ ਆਪੁ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਗਯੋ ਬਿਪ੍ਰ ਕੇ ਕਾਮ।","roman":"Athit bhekh saji aapu nrip gayo bipr ke kaam |","meaning_en":"Putting on the guise of a wandering guest, the king himself went, for the brahmin's sake,","page":1359,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਥਿਤ: a guest, a wandering mendicant.","meaning_pa":"ਜੋਗੀ ('ਅਤਿਥ') ਦਾ ਰੂਪ ਧਾਰ ਕੇ ਰਾਜਾ (ਬਿਕ੍ਰਮ) ਆਪ ਬ੍ਰਾਹਮਣ ਦੇ ਕੰਮ ਲਈ (ਉਥੇ) ਗਿਆ","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਹ ਕਾਮਾ ਲੋਟਤ ਹੁਤੀ ਲੈ ਮਾਧਵ ਕੋ ਨਾਮ। ੬੧।","roman":"Jah kaamaa lotat hutee lai maadhav ko naam | 61 |","meaning_en":"to where Kama lay rolling on the ground, taking Madhav's name.","page":1359,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਿਥੇ ਮਾਧਵਾਨਲ ਦਾ ਨਾ ਲੈ ਕੇ ਕਾਮਕੰਦਲਾ (ਤੜਪਦੀ ਹੋਈ) ਪਲਸੇਟੇ ਮਾਰ ਰਹੀ ਸੀ ॥੬੧॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":1359,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੌਪਈ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[62],"number_text":"੬੨।","page":1359,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਾਤੈ ਇਹੈ ਬਚਨ ਤਿਨ ਕਹਿਯੋ। ਮਾਧਵ ਖੇਤ ਹੇਤ ਤਵ ਰਹਿਯੋ।","roman":"Jaatai ihai bachan tin kahiyo | maadhav khet het tav rahiyo |","meaning_en":"On arriving he said these words: \"Madhav has fallen on the battlefield for your sake.\"","page":1359,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਖੇਤ ਰਹਿਯੋ: 'remained on the field', i.e. was killed.","meaning_pa":"ਜਾਦਿਆਂ ਹੀ ਉਸ ਨੂੰ ਇਹ ਬਚਨ ਕਿਹਾ ਕਿ ਮਾਧਵ ਤਾ ਤੇਰੇ ਲਈ ਲੜਾਈ ਵਿਚ ਮਾਰਿਆ ਗਿਆ ਹੈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਨਤ ਬਚਨ ਤਬ ਹੀ ਮਰਿ ਗਈ। ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਲੈ ਇਹੈ ਖਬਰਿ ਦਿਜ ਦਈ। ੬੨।","roman":"Sunat bachan tab hee mari gaee | nrip lai ihai khabri dij daee | 62 |","meaning_en":"Hearing the words, she died at once; the king took this news and gave it to the brahmin.","page":1359,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤਦ (ਇਹ) ਬੋਲ ਸੁਣਦਿਆਂ ਹੀ (ਕਾਮਕੰਦਲਾ) ਮਰ ਗਈ। (ਫਿਰ) ਰਾਜੇ ਨੇ ਇਹ ਖ਼ਬਰ ਲੈ ਕੇ ਬ੍ਰਾਹਮਣ ਨੂੰ ਜਾ ਦਿੱਤੀ ॥੬੨॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[63],"number_text":"੬੩।","page":1359,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਯਹ ਬਚ ਜਬ ਸ੍ਰੋਨਨ ਸੁਨਿ ਲੀਨੋ। ਪਲਕ ਏਕ ਮਹਿ ਪ੍ਰਾਨਹਿ ਦੀਨੋ।","roman":"Yah bach jab sronan suni leeno | palak ek mahi praanhi deeno |","meaning_en":"When he heard these words with his ears, in a moment he gave up his life.","page":1359,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਇਹ ਖ਼ਬਰ ਜਦ (ਮਾਧਵਾਨਲ ਨੇ) ਕੰਨਾ ਨਾਲ ਸੁਣ ਲਈ ਤਾ ਅੱਖ ਦੇ ਇਕ ਪਲਕਾਰੇ ਵਿਚ ਪ੍ਰਾਣ ਤਿਆਗ ਦਿੱਤੇ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਬ ਕੌਤਕ ਇਹ ਰਾਇ ਨਿਹਾਰਿਯੋ। ਜਰਨ ਮਰਨ ਕਾ ਨਿਗ੍ਰਹ ਧਾਰਿਯੋ। ੬੩।","roman":"Jab kautak ih raai nihaariyo | jaran maran kaa nigrah dhaariyo | 63 |","meaning_en":"When the king saw this strange event, he resolved to burn himself and die.","page":1359,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਦ ਰਾਜੇ ਨੇ ਇਹ ਕੌਤਕ ਵੇਖਿਆ ਤਾ ਸੜ ਕੇ ਮਰਨ ਦਾ ਹਠ ('ਨਿਗ੍ਰਹ') ਧਾਰਨ ਕਰ ਲਿਆ ॥੬੩॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[64],"number_text":"੬੪।","page":1359,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਚਿਤਾ ਜਰਾਇ ਜਰਨ ਜਬ ਲਾਗ੍ਯੋ। ਤਬ ਬੈਤਾਲ ਤਹਾ ਤੇ ਜਾਗ੍ਯੋ।","roman":"Chitaa jaraai jaran jab laagyo | tab baitaal tahaa te jaagyo |","meaning_en":"When he lit a pyre and was about to burn, then the Baital awoke there;","page":1359,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬੈਤਾਲ: the Vetal spirit who served King Vikram.","meaning_pa":"ਜਦ (ਰਾਜਾ) ਚਿਖਾ ਬਾਲ ਕੇ (ਉਸ ਵਿਚ) ਸੜਨ ਲਗਿਆ, ਤਾ ਉਥੋਂ ਇਕ ਬੈਤਾਲ ਜਾਗ ਪਿਆ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੰਚਿ ਅੰਮ੍ਰਿਤ ਤਿਹ ਦੁਹੂੰਨ ਜਿਯਾਯੋ। ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਕੇ ਚਿਤ ਕੋ ਤਾਪੁ ਮਿਟਾਯੋ। ੬੪।","roman":"Sanchi anmrit tih duhoonn jiyaayo | nrip ke chit ko taapu mitaayo | 64 |","meaning_en":"gathering nectar, he revived them both, and removed the anguish from the king's heart.","page":1359,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਸ ਨੇ ਅੰਮ੍ਰਿਤ ਛਿੜਕ ਕੇ ਦੋਹਾ ਨੂੰ ਜਿਵਾ ਦਿੱਤਾ ਅਤੇ ਰਾਜੇ ਦੇ ਮਨ ਦਾ ਦੁਖ ਦੂਰ ਕਰ ਦਿੱਤਾ ॥੬੪॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":1359,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[65,1],"number_text":"੬੫। ੧।","page":1359,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਹਿ ਸੈਥੀ ਪਾਵਕ ਬਰਿਯੋ ਦੁਹੂੰਅਨ ਲਯੋ ਬਚਾਇ।","roman":"Sahi saithee paavak bariyo duhoonan layo bachaai |","meaning_en":"He bore the lance, he entered the fire, he saved them both;","page":1359,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸੈਹਥੀ ਦਾ ਵਾਰ ਸਹਿ ਕੇ ਅਤੇ ਅੱਗ ਵਿਚ ਸੜ ਕੇ (ਰਾਜੇ ਨੇ) ਦੋਹਾ ਨੂੰ ਬਚਾ ਲਿਆ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਮਾ ਦਈ ਦਿਜੋਤ ਮਹਿ ਧੰਨ੍ਯੋ ਬਿਕ੍ਰਮਾਰਾਇ। ੬੫। ੧।","roman":"Kaamaa daee dijot mahi dhannyo bikramaaraai | 65 | 1 |","meaning_en":"he gave Kama to the brahmin; blessed is King Vikram.","page":1359,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਦਿਜੋਤ ਮਹਿ: printed so; read as 'to the brahmin'; uncertain."}]}],"ending":{"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਇਤਿ ਸ੍ਰੀ ਚਰਿਤ੍ਰ ਪਖ੍ਯਾਨੇ ਪੁਰਖ ਚਰਿਤ੍ਰੇ ਮੰਤ੍ਰੀ ਭੂਪ ਸੰਬਾਦੇ ਇਕਾਨਵੋ ਚਰਿਤ੍ਰ ਸਮਾਪਤਮ","roman":"Iti sree charitr pakhyaane purakh charitre mantree bhoop sanbaade ikaanvo charitr samaaptam","meaning_en":"Thus ends the ninety-first charitra of the Charitropakhyan, of the wiles of men, in the dialogue between the minister and the king,; complete.","page":1359,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਪੁਰਖ ਚਰਿਤ੍ਰ: the wiles (deeds) of men."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਤੁ ਸੁਭਮ ਸਤੁ। ੯੧। ੧੬੩੪। ਅਫਜੂੰ।","roman":"Satu subham satu | 91 | 1634 | aphjoon |","meaning_en":"True, auspicious, true. 91. 1634. It continues.","page":1359,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਫਜੂੰ: Persian afzun, 'increasing'.","meaning_pa":"ਸ੍ਰੇਸ਼ਠ ਬ੍ਰਾਹਮਣ ਨੂੰ ਕਾਮਕੰਦਲਾ ਦੇ ਦਿੱਤੀ। (ਸਚਮੁਚ) ਬਿਕ੍ਰਮਾਰਾਇ ਧੰਨ ਹੈ ॥੬੫॥ ਇਥੇ ਸ੍ਰੀ ਚਰਿਤ੍ਰੋਪਾਖਿਆਨ ਦੇ ਪੁਰਖ ਚਰਿਤ੍ਰ ਦੇ ਮੰਤ੍ਰੀ ਭੂਪ ਸੰਵਾਦ ਦੇ ੯੧ਵੇਾਂ ਚਰਿਤ੍ਰ ਦੀ ਸਮਾਪਤੀ, ਸਭ ਸ਼ੁਭ ਹੈ ॥੯੧॥੧੬੩੪॥ ਚਲਦਾ॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB","note_pa":"ਇਹ ਅਰਥ ਇਸ ਪੰਕਤੀ ਸਮੇਤ ਉੱਪਰਲੀਆਂ 3 ਪੰਕਤੀਆਂ ਦਾ ਇਕੱਠਾ ਹੈ।"}],"page":1359,"number":[91,1634]}});
